maia-httpd: switch DDC routing with a read-modify-write through the IIO driver

0001 switched DDC routing by mapping /dev/mem and writing the whole axi_ad9361
ADC GPIO register (core offset 0xBC) with 0 or 1. Only bit 0 is the routing
select: bits 1-2 drive the sync block and bit 3 the CS12 packer reset, so every
routing change also cleared them. The register belongs to the cf-ad9361-lpc
driver, and GET /api/ddc/config could not show the routing state (its
'enabled' field is the maia-sdr DDC input enable, a different thing).

Change only bit 0, in a read-modify-write under a mutex, and check the value
read back. The write goes through the cf-ad9361-lpc driver's debugfs register
interface (direct_reg_access with the core-register bit 31), where address and
value are a single write. The reads use a read-only /dev/mem mapping of the
core, whose base address is taken from sysfs: a debugfs read is two steps on
an address shared by every user of the file, and api_controller.sh polls
0x80000088 of the same device every 2 s, so about 0.4 percent of debugfs reads
of 0xBC return that register instead. Report the routing state in GET
/api/ddc/config as a new optional 'routing' field. The PATCH field stays
'enabled', so existing clients keep working.

